# Genuine locally fine sheaf acyclicity without compactness

Locally finite supported families are summed by actual sheaf gluing.
The resulting sums solve actual one-cocycles on arbitrary open covers.
The local additive Godement successor preserves the fine decomposition,
and its actual injective presentation shifts genuine Ext cohomology in
every degree.  Genuine smooth partitions instantiate the result for the
actual smooth complex-function sheaf on Hausdorff sigma-compact
finite-dimensional smooth real manifolds, including the noncompact
complex line and native two-dimensional complex affine space.

No solver, cohomological vanishing, or compactness assumption is made
for either affine-space endpoint.  This does not assert that the
holomorphic-function sheaf is fine.
